{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:97387","published":"2026-11-13T06:06:59.212490Z","modified":"2026-11-13T06:30:03.494179748Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-25679","CVE-2026-27137","CVE-2026-33811","CVE-2026-56859"],"summary":"Important: go-fdo-server security update","details":"This package provides a server-side implementation of the FIDO Device Onboard (FDO) specification, written in Go. FDO is an open standard for the late binding of device credentials, allowing for automated and secure on-boarding of devices when they are first powered on in their final location.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* crypto/x509: Incorrect enforcement of email constraints in crypto/x509 (CVE-2026-27137)\n\n* net/url: Incorrect parsing of IPv6 host literals in net/url (CVE-2026-25679)\n\n* net: golang: Go net package: Denial of Service via long CNAME response in LookupCNAME (CVE-2026-33811)\n\n* encoding/xml: golang: Go: Denial of Service via XML decoding recursion depth issue (CVE-2026-56859)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nAdditional Changes:\n\nFor detailed information on changes in this release, see the Rocky Linux 10 Release Notes linked from the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"go-fdo-server","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/go-fdo-server?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:1.0.1-6.el10_3"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:97387.json"}},{"package":{"name":"go-fdo-server-debuginfo","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/go-fdo-server-debuginfo?distro=rocky-linux-10&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:1.0.1-6.el10_3"}],"database_specific":{"yum_reposi